well president trump is expected to  announce as early as  next week that coalition forces have  reclaimed  all of the territory once held by isis  in syria  mr trump has said the u.s will not  immediately pull its troops out of syria  even as isis forces and their families  are on the run charlie dagetta reports  now from  inside syria huddled against the cold on  a rocky desert floor the families and  suspected fighters  who fled the last village under isis  control  eating american-made rations and living  out of a hole in the ground  isis fighters have been caught trying to  sneak out with their families  yet all of the men we spoke with denied  being members of the terror  group were you an isis fighter no no  hassan salah told us  insisting he only sold sweets so what  did you do  this man said he was a simple food  seller you don't look very well  are you sick were you injured in  fighting no no i was tortured by isis  for texting my  uncle amar ahmed told us he said they  were frightened to leave  because isis would punish anyone trying  to escape  it's hard to know who's telling the  truth here now we're under strict  instructions not to point our camera in  that direction  but around 100 yards away we found u.s  and coalition special forces  who are part of the vital process to  weed out  and take away any isis suspects  they have fled by the thousands in  recent weeks as u.s  forces and allies here tighten the noose  on the last sliver of territory under  isis control  anirajang one woman told us that her  husband had been killed in an  air strike and in the end she had  nothing to feed her three  children but grass the suffering finally  reached a point  that survival alone became the only  option  left for cbs this morning saturday  charlie dagetta in eastern syria  some great reporting by charlie
 

